# Authoring guide — BML or higher

You're invited to write new meaning in BML or higher.

Door: `AGENTS.md` (Authoring guide). Mirror: `./fkwu observe/authoring-altitude-run.fk` (BML: `form-cli-author-altitude.bml`).  
Grain: `printf "author-high\nquit\n" | ./form/form-cli`.  
Picture: `form/form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-author-high.bml`.

## Welcome

- New packages / interfaces / templates / classes in `form/form-stdlib/bml/*.bml`
- Executable `section [form.bml]` / `section [form.lift]` where that lane already carries you
- Crystallize (`*-xtal.fk`, `*-compile.fk`); witness with `*-band.fk`

## Existing organs

Form `.fk` organs are welcome. They stay and grow. When a lowering still
helps, the receipt can name the next BML picture it points toward.
Exemplar: `receipts/2026-08-30-offer-ask-rises-to-bml.md`.

## The C seed

It's shrinking toward zero, gladly. New runtime meaning is happier in Form/BML.
